      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for inpatients. It's also eight times the OTC limit of 1,200 mg/day. At that dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove them.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg total per day**, divided into 400 mg \u00d7 4 or 800 mg \u00d7 2\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I'll enter it with that note. Otherwise, tell me which dose to enter."
      }
